description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts, compose lessons are recalled from concept-db and injected into the drafter prompt, but their usage is never recorded, so every compose_lesson concept sits at times_succeeded=0 AND times_failed=0 forever and the lesson corpus cannot be graded at all.

Make the failure half of that credit real, in this one file. A previous attempt failed with TS2339 because it read an id off a row type that does not declare one, so the type annotation must be widened as part of this change.

Anchor one — these two consecutive lines occur exactly once, at the concept-db recall:

        const json = (await resp.json()) as { content?: Array<{ content?: string }> };
        const found = (json.content ?? []).map((c) => c.content).filter((s): s is string => typeof s === "string" && s.length > 0);

Widen that type annotation so each row also declares an optional string id, and alongside building `found`, build a list of the row ids that are present (skipping rows without one). Store that id list in a module-scoped array declared near COMPOSE_LESSONS_PATH, resetting it at the start of each recall so it always reflects the current compose.

Anchor two — this line occurs exactly once and runs when a compose has definitively FAILED with a known failure class:

      lessons.push({ at: new Date().toISOString(), class: cls, reason: diag.slice(0, 200), raw_excerpt: diag.slice(0, 1500) });

Immediately after that line, record a usage outcome of failure against each concept id in that module-scoped array by POSTing to concept-db's per-concept usage endpoint, reusing the same concept-db base URL and the same ApiKey header built from METABOB_API_KEY that the recall above already uses. Make it best-effort and non-fatal — wrap it so a concept-db error or timeout can never fail or delay the compose, exactly as the existing recall already fails open.

This is deliberately the failure half only; success crediting depends on the landing outcome, which lives in another file, and is out of scope. Change nothing else in this file.

